<assessmentItem xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqti_v2p1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqti_v2p1 https://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqti_v2p1p2.xsd" identifier="order-reference" title="order-reference" adaptive="false" timeDependent="false" xml:lang="en">
  <responseDeclaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" baseType="string"></responseDeclaration>
  <outcomeDeclaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" baseType="float"><defaultValue><value>0</value></defaultValue></outcomeDeclaration>

  <itemBody><p>A science-planning item asks the student to arrange investigation steps in order.</p><extendedTextInteraction responseIdentifier="RESPONSE"><prompt>A science class is planning a fair test of how light affects seedling growth. Put the investigation steps in the best order.<div><p>Source options:</p><ul><li>Set up identical trays with the same soil, seed type, and water schedule.</li><li>Place one tray in full light and one tray in reduced light for the same number of days.</li><li>Measure and compare seedling height at the end of the trial.</li><li>Use the measurements to write a conclusion about how light affected growth.</li></ul></div></prompt></extendedTextInteraction></itemBody>

</assessmentItem>",
}
`;

